Package: FMLE
Type: Package
Title: Fuzzy mixture of linear experts for regime-aware RNA-to-protein prediction
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Vikas", "Singh",
           email = "vikkysingh07@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Implements Fuzzy Mixture of Linear Experts (FMLE) for
    regime-aware prediction of surface protein abundance from single-cell
    transcriptomic features, as measured, for example, in CITE-seq
    experiments. FMLE models protein abundance as a soft mixture of
    cell-state-dependent RNA-to-protein mappings with input-dependent
    gating, allowing RNA--protein coupling to vary across cellular
    contexts rather than enforcing a single global relationship. The
    package supports single-protein prediction, cross-validation,
    uncertainty decomposition, and preprocessing utilities for Seurat-
    based single-cell workflows. Although implemented in a general
    regression framework, the primary focus is accurate and interpretable
    protein prediction, identification of reproducible coupling regimes,
    and analysis of context-dependent RNA--protein relationships across
    donors, batches, and transfer settings in single-cell multimodal
    data.    
